# looot agent token. Server side only, never sent to the browser.
# Create one with `looot login`, or in the looot web app under Settings, "Agent tokens".
# Needed for a real run. Not needed for --demo, --dry-run or `npm run demo`.
LOOOT_TOKEN=your-looot-agent-token
# Optional, defaults to https://api.looot.ai
# LOOOT_API_URL=https://api.looot.ai
# Optional, adds a model-written summary to each card when you pass --summary
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional, model for the summary. Default claude-sonnet-5-5
# BATTLECARDS_LLM_MODEL=
# Optional, where the web UI reads and writes cards. Default: ./cards
# CARDS_DIR=cards
# Admin password for the web UI: every page and API route except the public ones (sign-in, health). 12 characters or more.
# Required outside the demo. Without it the admin pages stay closed and /login shows a setup page.
BATTLECARDS_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Alternative to the plain password: the output of `npm run hash-password -- 'your password'`. Wins if both are set.
# BATTLECARDS_ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=
# Optional. Key that signs session cookies. Default: derived from the password, so a new password signs everyone out.
# BATTLECARDS_SESSION_SECRET=
# Optional. Set to 0 only to test over plain http in production mode. Leave unset otherwise.
# BATTLECARDS_COOKIE_SECURE=
# Optional. Spend cap in dollars for one web build. Default 1. A request cannot change it.
# BATTLECARDS_MAX_SPEND_USD=1
